zk-audit

This project adapts ideas, structure and some text from the MIT-licensed
projects listed below. Files that contain adapted text carry a short header
comment naming the upstream project. The upstream copyright notices and the
MIT permission notice are reproduced here as those licenses require.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
zkSecurity zk-skills (circom-auditor)
https://github.com/zksecurity/zk-skills
Copyright (c) 2026 zkSecurity
License: MIT

Adapted: senior-auditor SOP (Feynman / Socratic / Inversion triggers),
shared-rules output blocks (FINDING needs proof, otherwise LEAD), the four
judging gates, vector-scan Skip/Drop/Investigate classification, gap-hunter
seam pattern, bundle-per-agent orchestration with bounded concurrency, and
the generic ZK vector families rewritten for gnark.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pashov skills (solidity-auditor, x-ray)
https://github.com/pashov/skills
Copyright (c) 2024 AI Skills Contributors
License: MIT

Adapted: judging gates and confidence deductions, lead promotion rules,
dedup rules (function isolation, fix-option preservation, completeness
check), the asymmetry lens, the read-only clause for agents, the
deterministic report-assembly principle and the coverage-honesty rule.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cloudflare security-audit-skill
https://github.com/cloudflare/security-audit-skill
Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Cloudflare, Inc.
License: MIT

Adapted: guidance mode vs full-audit mode, output outside the target repo,
quick/standard/deep profiles, coverage ledger of deterministic units checked
by a validator, coverage critic, the "you did not write this candidate"
verifier stance, and the confirmed / needs_validation / rejected verdict
schema.

